    "interpretation": "All eight calls passed the probe exact-output checks, retaining rows ? columns nonzero outputs for each shape. Candidate pooled GPU time was lower in both synthetic 128-column cases. This is a short screen with two interleaved calls per arm and 40 measured samples per arm/shape, with observed other-GPU, CPU, process, and disk activity. It establishes no model effect or performance gate result. The container exited 137 during intentional cleanup after all eight calls completed with exit 0.",
    "limitations": [
      "Synthetic matrices only; both cases have 128 columns.",
      "Not model/HF, depth, split, or end-to-end performance evidence.",
      "No performance qualification or gate decision.",
      "One-second monitor sampling can miss short-lived activity; all raw monitoring and calls are retained."
    ],
    "width_split_invariants": {
      "conclusion": "For valid NVFP4 Vulkan matrix calls, every row width is a multiple of 64 and each NVFP4 K part and stage ends on a valid boundary. The grouped load may omit per-element k < nin checks. An xin-false path must still initialize its shared pairs, for example by writing zeros.",
      "source_anchors": [
        {
          "path": "src/quant/types.hpp",
          "lines": "86-87, 121",
          "sha256": "0573cd81ba86b7630400b637447b3fdb20acf612b7415fe9e83d6f9e949e85bd",
          "evidence": "NVFP4 block size is 64; row_bytes rejects nin not divisible by the storage block size."
        },
        {
          "path": "src/backends/vulkan/vulkan_matmul.hpp",
          "lines": "158-163, 626-635",
          "sha256": "f807d6a678cafffb8cb386b6fab8f5b90854fcf29cc1adbc7ec40cf18b18a218",
          "evidence": "Float tile uses steps=ceil(nin/32). split_blocks rounds K part size to an even count of 32-value steps, capped at nblk=nin/32, which is even for valid NVFP4 widths."
        },
        {
          "path": "src/backends/vulkan/shaders/matmul_tile.comp",
          "lines": "100-105, 462-486",
          "sha256": "e68a3eb5c9938252fa5243601d822b274775543b0e678a6452f674806eda9d6c",
          "evidence": "NVFP4 STAGE_K is 32 and XPR is 4. Input loops advance exactly one 32-value stage; xin still gates columns. The current per-value K predicate is redundant under the host width/split invariants."
        },
        {
          "path": "src/backends/vulkan/vulkan_matmul.hpp",
          "lines": "553-560",
          "sha256": "f807d6a678cafffb8cb386b6fab8f5b90854fcf29cc1adbc7ec40cf18b18a218",
          "evidence": "Routed float-tile dispatch uses the same checked matrix width and does not K-split in this path."
        }
      ],
      "caveat": "The proof concerns paths that pass check_matrix/row_bytes. Preserve zero initialization for invalid xin columns because shared memory is consumed before output stores suppress invalid columns."
    }
  },
